HTTP Methods && STATUS Codes
-------------------------------------------------
(i) GET -- > Get or fetch data from server
           If you open a website, browser sends a GET request
(ii) POST --> posting or sending the information to the server.
           Filling a signup form → data is saved in database
(iii) PUT --> Used to update existing data completely
          Updating your full profile (name, email, phone all together)
(iv) DELETE --> Used to delete data from server
          Deleting your account
******************************
Better understanding with simple real life example of “Food Order”
GET → See menu
POST → Order food
PUT → Change entire order
DELETE → Cancel order

STATUS CODE
*************************
1** -- > Informational
---------------------------------
100 -> continue --- wait I’m processing.
******************
2** -- > Success
-----------------------------
200 -> OK --- Everything worked fine
201 -> created --- New data created
204 -> No content ---- Success but no data to return
_________________________________
3** --> Redirectional
--------------------------------------
301 -> Moved permanantly --- URL changed permanently
302 - > Found ---- Temporary redirect
*********************************
4** --> Client Errors
-----------------------------------------
400 -> Bad request ---- Wrong request format
401 -> Unauthorized ---- Login required
403 -> Forbidden ---- No permission
404 -> Not found --- resource not found
******************************
5** --> Server errors
----------------------------------------
500 -> Internal Server Error --- Server crashed
502 -> Bad gateway --- Server got wrong response
503 - > Service Unavailable --- Server is down
***********************************
Better understanding with simple real life example of “Food Order”
-----------------------------------------------
200 → Your food is served
201 → New order created
404 → Item not on menu
403 → You’re not allowed
500 → Chef messed up
